s it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\n- [ ] A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\n- [ ] Lint clean\n- [ ] Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\n- [ ] New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\n- [ ] Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\n\n## Task\n\n- **ID:** TASK-260830-21gygk\n- **Title:** TASK-260830-21gygk: implement-name-resolution-and-summary\n- **Parent:** STORY-260830-3tq4ns\n\n### Description\n\nResolve UUID/name/qualified selectors, ambiguity, list/status summaries, and stable deterministic sorting. This is an implementation deliverable, not a specification rewrite.\n\n### Scope\n\nAdopted current authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0, commit 0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6. Primary owner of sections 14.7 and 14.7.1 and shared SelectionPlan construction/revalidation in 14.7.2, refining section 2.3 and authoritative summaries in 5.7/14.7.3. Implement first-at literal grammar, exact source mappings, complete source reads with distinct failure classes, no explicit-source fallback, tier/collision/tombstone semantics, immutable locally attested plan and current-fact validation. Expose one shared API; CLI/lifecycle callers own invoking it at every required boundary, never a duplicate resolver. Historical scope retained without weakening: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.5.0 (commit 28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c); \\u00a72.3, \\u00a75.1-5.2, \\u00a75.7, \\u00a714.4. Work only inside the session-state-projection-and-name-resolution story boundary. Activation waits for signed STORY-260908-18woqo landing; this binding does not accept or alter the preserved partial implementation.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\nProduction behavior demonstrates: Resolve UUID/name/qualified selectors, ambiguity, list/status summaries, and stable deterministic sorting. Exact contract fixtures and negative/refusal cases pass; crash/idempotency evidence is included when the operation mutates durable state; no unsupported capability is advertised.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_primary-summary-prefix-clarification.md\n> Pinned bootstrap prefix constraints for future public summary review\n\nPrimary read-only clarification of the partial public-summary bound: pinned SPEC Section5.7 (internal/specdoc/SPEC.md:2277) defines creating as Session Record AND initial lease existing, and Section13.1 step2 (8117) persists initial Lease Record and session.created before process creation. The partial bounds_test.go comment claiming a valid creating session has no owner event is not sufficient evidence that record-only/no-lease projection is a valid public creating state. Distinguish an interrupted persistence prefix from a completed bootstrap prefix; reconcile the accepted projector empty-chain behavior with these exact normative requirements in future scoped review. No accepted CR is invalidated by this note, no replacement state/error invented, and no nullable/placeholder owner or lease fields authorized. Public-summary observation owners and qualified-selector decision remain outstanding; original task scope is unchanged. This is a routing clarification, not tested product repair or acceptance.\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_resume-v060.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_resume-v060.md`\n\n- Byte count: `3266`\n- Content digest: `sha256:9bf56cdfdea9340a24a9b8e0ddc69b9772f799f86f29fa469b1433e7c9194045`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-v060.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-v060.md`\n\n- Byte count: `3155`\n- Content digest: `sha256:d735f00276e7d5753b3ef10553acbcf12f75792f1282773d3062b4f29a5d7921`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_resume-pr202.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_resume-pr202.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2263`\n- Content digest: `sha256:d4ce8acb26093ecaa9bac0f40dd251c4f867e28b09dd8a185bf2fa20e0fa8c5e`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_resume-bound-replay.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_resume-bound-replay.md`\n\n- Byte count: `3175`\n- Content digest: `sha256:0b52215f5b63938fe52e20c2234576da09a0b86b0e3b6139abed7e524aa787ac`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-bd27d9-addendum.md\nReview addendum for the actual CR produced by RUN-260909-bd27d9. Read alongside TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-v060.md; this adds evidence questions and does not waive any acceptance criterion.\n\nThe latest producer outcome explicitly says authority_heads binds only event-head digests of the selected plan source and union precedence facts are not rechecked. Compare that declared limitation against every applicable v0.6.0 SelectionPlan/revalidation requirement; prove correct behavior when another allowed source changes the authoritative winner after BuildPlan. Do not treat a declared limitation as a scope exemption. Likewise inspect lease_record_id substitution and claimed caller ownership of 14.7.3 shared summary refusal.\n\nThe latest mutant outcome reports only control-before/control-after green, C-not-applied and C-compile-failure classifications. Those do not themselves demonstrate a SURVIVED result through the same instrument. Inspect actual durable harness evidence and classify claims precisely; no requirement to repeat a battery whose valid exact-candidate evidence is already complete.\n\nThe source-owned checkpoint refresh completed at signed branch83640d191f78f0cd685e5f709027819799efe1cf over main8cf4aaaa190e6a11dff2661aa6806ce476128653. Review the actual CR, including replayed predecessor preservation and LOGBOOK resolution. A stray untracked --help/mutation-source tree was preserved under ignored task scratch; it must not enter the candidate diff.\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_resume-resources-204.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_resume-resources-204.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2318`\n- Content digest: `sha256:e91f44d930c3b6a76030e816106a8fb17475db5e54f5fa5a6459d25390864e22`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-ffb76b.md\nReview the actual ready immutable CR for TASK-260830-21gygk after RUN-260909-ffb76b. Read attached TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-v060.md and TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-bd27d9-addendum.md in full; their complete assigned scope and independent-review requirements remain active.\n\nRead latest TASK-260830-21gygk_results-ffb76b.md, validation-ffb76b.log, revalidation-probe-ffb76b.log and mutants-bd27d9.json. Producer changed no product code during publication recovery. PR204 restored missing protected resource JSON; command24 passed independently, but require actual ready CR and its final validation result.\n\nP1/P2 now have concrete production diagnostic observations: fresh Resolve changes the peer-tier name winner after a local same-name gain, or refuses cross-source record divergence, while Revalidate(old plan) returns nil. P3 selected-source change correctly refuses. Producer argues pinned UUID/provenance and prohibition on name re-resolution make this correct; evaluate the normative text yourself, distinguishing forbidden retargeting from required refusal and all complete-authority requirements. Diagnostic PASS is not a correctness test.\n\nProducer explicitly declares lease_record_id absent, not equivalent, because this stack lacks Lease Record objects, and assigns it to a later caller leaf. Independently determine whether that preserves the assigned shared SelectionPlan requirement or leaves an acceptance gap. Do not waive a required field solely because its dependency is missing; do not invent a digest. Likewise assess claimed caller ownership of 14.7.3 versus shared summary scope. Preserve the full objective and actual ownership contracts.\n\nIf evidence is insufficient or requirements unmet, record precise changes requested through the normal review lifecycle. Do not edit product files or land. Only accept_cr after independent evidence and the live merged reviewer checklist satisfy the actual immutable candidate.\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev2.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev2.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2954`\n- Content digest: `sha256:cc9d0c6213b6c20be3ccb0ca0cf36fa0b7e1ad364490a8f63f75c1e7450fd684`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-rework.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-rework.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2250`\n- Content digest: `sha256:823e49e2976d49e3280051b1a56077082292b9f4d9d0b6ae99756a49a99372af`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev3.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev3.md`\n\n- Byte count: `3766`\n- Content digest: `sha256:fd4290438b9261388b7d53247939f1986766bdf80b6db839d221c89bb57060e0`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-after-b4446d.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-after-b4446d.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2854`\n- Content digest: `sha256:6af3fe42ef9c869e05dd43d7cfacbe7db9c702a84c99a53ecec31fb0d2b3cf31`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_recover-handoff-260910.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_recover-handoff-260910.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2126`\n- Content digest: `sha256:61d778f704c877562d8ab72194e0e2ba49b35c049494bdead43d98bb5b5cdda2`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-rev4.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-rev4.md`\n\n- Byte count: `3254`\n- Content digest: `sha256:98512f44d8118c96fd8a9cfea548c6d3c442328a13902e6b602eac76f8ef82d6`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev4.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev4.md`\n\n- Byte count: `3920`\n- Content digest: `sha256:67fe5f8e7be6985809478ed766a1d09409258b0d3f8415b1185d270432780f63`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-after-37e5e2.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-after-37e5e2.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2194`\n- Content digest: `sha256:bde6cee74979c29c1c9308f0b196269363090baac23ac7b98c9b2d690cdcc897`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev5.md\nRework CR5 preserving the complete assigned scope and existing candidate in the managed Story worktree. Read TASK-260830-21gygk_review-verdict-rev5.md and materialize TASK-260830-21gygk_review-evidence-rev5.tar.gz. Port the reviewer production regressions first, record their failing baseline, then fix the shared semantic admission path.\nThe recurring defect family is canonical identity mistaken for semantic authority. Audit the pinned 5.3/5.4 requirements across the whole winning ancestry before changing code: every necessary ancestor checkpoint must be admitted, and checkpoint created_by_host_id must match its owning lease holder. Drive positive multi-generation control and missing/wrong ancestor checkpoint and wrong creator negatives through BuildPlan, old-plan Revalidate, AuthoritativeStatus and AuthoritativeList. Preserve valid branching, lagging copies, canonical identity, required parked-source refusal and all seven capability names. Do not reopen closed prior review findings or reduce the task/AC denominator. Add focused qualifying narrowing mutants for these missing semantic guards with actual applied passing survivor through the same instrument. Bind evidence to final source and correct the prior gofmt command exit-2 description (absent cmd directory); do not claim old failed evidence clean. Retain full local required validation. No hosted CI. Handoff an uncommitted complete candidate via normal task-board CR lifecycle for independent review; no manual integration or destructive Git commands.\n\n\n\n\n\n## Evidence and Safety\n\n- Add/update a task-scoped outcome named `TASK-260830-21gygk_*` before handoff:\n  `task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260830-21gygk, name=TASK-260830-21gygk_results.md, content=\"...\", type=outcome, description=\"Handoff evidence\")'`\n- Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior ships with negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; prove the bound by narrowing it, not only by deleting it, and name the production call site. Shapes and incidents: `references/negative-evidence.md`.\n- An absence and a failure to read are different facts; report unknown instead of inferring a property from a proxy signal.\n- Stop-The-Line only for an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved human-only product/platform/architecture/approval decision. Persist evidence, failed attempts, options/tradeoffs, recommendation, and exact input needed; otherwise rework autonomously.\n- `to-review` is a role handoff, not accepted completion. Report **ready for review** or **handed off to review**.\n\n## LAST — Run For Role Handoff\n\nAfter AC, checklist, validation, and outcome evidence:\n\n```bash\ntask-board handoff TASK-260830-21gygk --role developer\n```\n\n## Working Directory\nBoard directory: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board`\n\nWork in the project root. Never edit board files directly.\n\n## Story Workspace\n\nYou are running in an isolated Git worktree for STORY-260830-3tq4ns.\n\n- Workspace path: `.temp/STORY-260830-3tq4ns/worktree` (this is your working directory)\n- Branch: `task-board/story/STORY-260830-3tq4ns`, forked from `main`\n- Authoritative board: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board` (already exported as `TASK_BOARD_DIR`)\n\nMake every repository change here. Do not commit, switch, rebase, merge, or delete this branch, and do not run `task-board` against the `.task-board` copy inside this worktree — it is a checkout artifact, not the board. Integration into trunk is the orchestrator's step, not yours.\n\nLeave your work UNCOMMITTED in the worktree — the handoff snapshots the working tree against the recorded checkpoint. A commit of your own on this branch is refused at handoff with `change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint`, and the repair is `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n"}}
