{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c78b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08902-6908-7901-ad83-4a5ad2f4cb7e"},"sequence":544,"recorded_at":1780531400001083,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"c06b7799-3d10-4fbc-bddd-7d86f5813b0c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"c06b7799-3d10-4fbc-bddd-7d86f5813b0c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"c06b7799-3d10-4fbc-bddd-7d86f5813b0c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a08903-80f8-7471-9521-2dd80b000e47"},"task_id":"01a08903-80f8-7471-9521-2dd80b000e47","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a08903-80f8-7471-9521-2dd80b000e47","chunk":"Read text file `internal/sessquery/plan.go`.\n1|// Immutable SelectionPlan construction and current-fact revalidation\n2|// for the v0.6.0 selector contract (SPEC Section 14.7.2).\n3|//\n4|// Resolve the key to a session UUID once per invocation or confirmed\n5|// plan, then bind the selection facts into a machine-local immutable\n6|// plan: the literal selector, the selected session and its validated\n7|// immutable record digest, the selected source (host and exact alias),\n8|// the digests of the complete validated index read and the effective\n9|// validated configuration, the validated winning lease facts, the\n10|// validated authority heads, and the caller-declared action,\n11|// destination, and expectations. No plan hash, name, source, or display\n12|// field is a capability. All sixteen contract members bind; a future\n13|// member without a bound row fails its publication gate closed instead\n14|// of falling into a default.\n15|//\n16|// Lease authority comes from validated urn:ax:schema:lease records\n17|// supplied in Reader.LeaseRecords and admitted through the\n18|// canonicaljson owner. The plan binds lease_record_id as the canonical\n19|// digest of the winning Lease Record for the selected session, and the\n20|// lease triple binds from that same record. No envelope observation\n21|// substitutes for the record: a session with no admitted winning\n22|// record refuses selector_observation_unavailable, and malformed bytes\n23|// refuse invalid_config. A complete read proving a record without any\n24|// valid lease refuses selector_bootstrap_incomplete instead of binding\n25|// an empty triple, and a local selection without a known local host\n26|// refuses invalid_config instead of binding an empty source host.\n27|//\n28|// Revalidation rereads the current configuration and the plan's source,\n29|// validates the same immutable record, the current winning lease, and\n30|// the action prerequisites this leaf can check, compares every bound\n31|// plan fact in a fixed order, and then validates the complete\n32|// authority union for the pinned session UUID across the local and\n33|// every allowlisted source: a contradictory immutable record is\n34|// integrity failure, a contradictory winning lease or fresh tombstone\n35|// evidence is stale. A changed mapping, alias, allowlist, transport,\n36|// source index, record, authority head, lease, action, destination, or\n37|// expectation invalidates the plan with selector_plan_stale naming the\n38|// first diverged member; explicit authorization revocation returns\n39|// peer_not_allowlisted; failed reads retain their read-failure\n40|// classification. Revalidation never re-resolves by name, substitutes\n41|// a same-named session, silently replans, transfers a lease, or reuses\n42|// confirmation for new facts.\n43|//\n44|// Effect authorization beyond read projection — fencing, commit,\n45|// retry, recovery, remote dispatch/admission, and transport-resume\n46|// prerequisites, and the composed per-endpoint invocation bindings —\n47|// belongs to the CLI and lifecycle owners, which invoke Revalidate at\n48|// every boundary in BoundariesFor for their action. A plan built here\n49|// authorizes read projection only.\n50|package sessquery\n51|\n52|import (\n53|\t\"fmt\"\n54|\n55|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n56|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n57|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessstate\"\n58|)\n59|\n60|// SelectorVersion is the exact selector contract version every plan binds.\n61|const SelectorVersion = \"1.0.0\"\n62|\n63|// Plan actions admitted by the Section 14.7.2 boundary matrix. Each is\n64|// an existing command/action tag; binding one selects it, never an\n65|// umbrella bypass.\n66|const (\n67|\tActionStatus      = \"status\"\n68|\tActionAttach      = \"attach\"\n69|\tActionTakeover    = \"takeover\"\n70|\tActionFork        = \"fork\"\n71|\tActionStop        = \"stop\"\n72|\tActionResume      = \"resume\"\n73|\tActionSync        = \"sync\"\n74|\tActionDiff        = \"diff\"\n75|\tActionMaterialize = \"materialize\"\n76|\tActionSetProfile  = \"session.set-profile\"\n77|\tActionLogs        = \"logs\"\n78|\tActionCancel      = \"cancel\"\n79|)\n80|\n81|// Plan boundaries from the normative action/boundary matrix. A boundary\n82|// is reached only when the existing operation reaches that phase; these\n83|// rows introduce no new effects.\n84|const (\n85|\tBoundaryProjection      = \"projection\"\n86|\tBoundaryPreEffect       = \"pre-effect\"\n87|\tBoundaryFencing         = \"fencing\"\n88|\tBoundaryCommit          = \"commit\"\n89|\tBoundaryRetry           = \"retry\"\n90|\tBoundaryRecovery        = \"recovery\"\n91|\tBoundaryRemoteDispatch  = \"remote-dispatch\"\n92|\tBoundaryRemoteAdmission = \"remote-admission\"\n93|\tBoundaryTransportResume = \"transport-resume\"\n94|)\n95|\n96|// planBoundaries is the closed action/boundary matrix: every action has\n97|// exactly its normative row, and an unknown action has none.\n98|var planBoundaries = map[string][]string{\n99|\tActionStatus:      {BoundaryProjection, BoundaryRetry},\n100|\tActionAttach:      {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRemoteDispatch, BoundaryRemoteAdmission, BoundaryTransportResume},\n101|\tActionTakeover:    {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryCommit, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRecovery, BoundaryTransportResume},\n102|\tActionFork:        {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryCommit, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRecovery, BoundaryTransportResume},\n103|\tActionStop:        {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryCommit, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRecovery, BoundaryTransportResume},\n104|\tActionResume:      {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryCommit, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRecovery, BoundaryTransportResume},\n105|\tActionSync:        {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryCommit, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRecovery, BoundaryTransportResume},\n106|\tActionDiff:        {BoundaryProjection, BoundaryRetry},\n107|\tActionMaterialize: {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryCommit, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRecovery},\n108|\tActionSetProfile:  {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryCommit, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRecovery},\n109|\tActionLogs:        {BoundaryProjection, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRemoteDispatch, BoundaryRemoteAdmission, BoundaryTransportResume},\n110|\tActionCancel:      {BoundaryProjection},\n111|}\n112|\n113|// BoundariesFor returns the required boundary classes for a plan\n114|// action. The boolean reports whether the action is a known tag; an\n115|// unknown action binds no boundary and builds no plan.\n116|func BoundariesFor(action string) ([]string, bool) {\n117|\tboundaries, ok := planBoundaries[action]\n118|\tif !ok {\n119|\t\treturn nil, false\n120|\t}\n121|\treturn append([]string(nil), boundaries...), true\n122|}\n123|\n124|// SelectionPlan is the machine-local immutable binding of one selector\n125|// resolution. All members are values, never references: there is no\n126|// mutator, and Marshal carries the locally verified canonical digest\n127|// so a persisted plan is tamper-evident. Caller-supplied digest\n128|// equality alone is never evidence of authority; only Revalidate\n129|// against current facts decides currency.\n130|type SelectionPlan struct {\n131|\t// SelectorVersion is exactly SelectorVersion.\n132|\tSelectorVersion string\n133|\t// Selector is the original single argument, at most\n134|\t// MaxSelectorRunes characters.\n135|\tSelector string\n136|\t// SessionID is the selected UUIDv7, never resolved again by name.\n137|\tSessionID string\n138|\t// SessionRecordID is the validated immutable Session Record digest.\n139|\tSessionRecordID string\n140|\t// SourceHostID is the UUIDv7 of the selected source, always bound:\n141|\t// a local selection without a known local host refuses\n142|\t// invalid_config at build time instead of binding empty.\n143|\tSourceHostID string\n144|\t// SourceAlias is the exact configured alias, or nil for local. It\n145|\t// is a diagnostic label, never identity.\n146|\tSourceAlias *string\n147|\t// SourceIndexDigest is the digest of the complete validated index\n148|\t// read used for selection.\n149|\tSourceIndexDigest string\n150|\t// ConfigurationDigest is the digest of the effective validated\n151|\t// configuration, including peer mapping, allowlist, and transport.\n152|\tConfigurationDigest string\n153|\t// LeaseRecordID is the canonical digest of the validated winning\n154|\t// Lease Record for the selected session, admitted through the\n155|\t// canonicaljson owner from Reader.LeaseRecords.\n156|\tLeaseRecordID string\n157|\t// LeaseEpoch, LeaseID, and OwnerHostID come from that same winning\n158|\t// Lease Record: positive uint53, UUIDv4, and UUIDv7 holder. A plan\n159|\t// with no admitted winning record is never built; the builder\n160|\t// refuses selector_observation_unavailable, and a complete read\n161|\t// proving a record without any valid lease refuses\n162|\t// selector_bootstrap_incomplete.\n163|\tLeaseEpoch  uint64\n164|\tLeaseID     string\n165|\tOwnerHostID string\n166|\t// AuthorityHeads is the sorted unique digest array of the validated\n167|\t// lease, event, and tombstone heads used for the decision: the\n168|\t// winning Lease Record digest plus the tail event digest of every\n169|\t// allowed source holding a non-parked copy of the pinned session.\n170|\tAuthorityHeads []string\n171|\t// Action is the explicit command/action tag bound at build time.\n172|\tAction string\n173|\t// DestinationHostID is the explicit destination UUIDv7, or nil\n174|\t// when the action takes no destination.\n175|\tDestinationHostID *string\n176|\t// ExpectationDigest binds the caller-declared action expectations\n177|\t// (canonically encoded JSON) for change detection. It does not\n178|\t// replace the checkpoint, workspace, cohort, provider, terminal,\n179|\t// or confirmation contracts, which have no owners in this leaf.\n180|\tExpectationDigest string\n181|}\n182|\n183|// PlanArgs declares the invocation facts BuildPlan binds: the literal\n184|// selector, the explicit action tag, the explicit destination (empty\n185|// for none), and the opaque caller expectations (nil for none).\n186|type PlanArgs struct {\n187|\tSelector     string\n188|\tAction       string\n189|\tDestination  string\n190|\tExpectations []byte\n191|}\n192|\n193|// BuildPlan resolves the selector once through the shared path and\n194|// binds the current facts into an immutable plan. The destination is\n195|// independently validated as a UUIDv7; expectations must be canonically\n196|// encodable JSON and bind by digest for change detection only.\n197|func (reader *Reader) BuildPlan(args PlanArgs) (SelectionPlan, error) {\n198|\tparsed, err := ParseSelector(args.Selector)\n199|\tif err != nil {\n200|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n201|\t}\n202|\tif reader == nil || reader.Local == nil {\n203|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: local repository is required\", ErrUnavailable)\n204|\t}\n205|\tconfig, err := reader.validatedConfiguration()\n206|\tif err != nil {\n207|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n208|\t}\n209|\tif _, ok := BoundariesFor(args.Action); !ok {\n210|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: unknown plan action %q\", ErrInvalidArgument, args.Action)\n211|\t}\n212|\tvar destination *string\n213|\tif args.Destination != \"\" {\n214|\t\tid, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(args.Destination)\n215|\t\tif err != nil {\n216|\t\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: malformed destination host ID: %v\", ErrInvalidArgument, err)\n217|\t\t}\n218|\t\tvalue := id.String()\n219|\t\tdestination = &value\n220|\t}\n221|\texpectations, err := fingerprintExpectations(args.Expectations)\n222|\tif err != nil {\n223|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n224|\t}\n225|\tvar selected Selection\n226|\tif parsed.Source != SourceBare {\n227|\t\tselected, err = reader.resolveExplicit(parsed, config)\n228|\t} else {\n229|\t\tselected, err = reader.resolveBare(parsed, config)\n230|\t}\n231|\tif err != nil {\n232|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n233|\t}\n234|\treturn reader.bindPlan(parsed, config, selected, args.Action, destination, expectations)\n235|}\n236|\n237|// bindPlan reads the winning source completely and binds every plan\n238|// member from validated current facts. The session is located by its\n239|// UUID in the winning source only, never re-resolved by name. Lease\n240|// authority comes from the admitted winning Lease Record for that\n241|// UUID; the envelope winner on the selected chain must agree with it,\n242|// and the union winner across all allowed sources must not exceed it.\n243|func (reader *Reader) bindPlan(parsed Selector, config validatedConfig, selected Selection, action string, destination *string, expectations string) (SelectionPlan, error) {\n244|\trows, err := reader.readSource(selected.repo, selected.PeerHostID)\n245|\tif err != nil {\n246|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n247|\t}\n248|\tindex, err := fingerprintIndex(reader, selected.repo, rows, selected.PeerHostID)\n249|\tif err != nil {\n250|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n251|\t}\n252|\tconfiguration, err := fingerprintConfiguration(reader, config)\n253|\tif err != nil {\n254|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n255|\t}\n256|\tvar recordID string\n257|\tfound := false\n258|\tfor _, row := range rows {\n259|\t\tif row.Projection.SessionID == selected.SessionID {\n260|\t\t\trecordID, found = row.Projection.RecordID, true\n261|\t\t\tbreak\n262|\t\t}\n263|\t}\n264|\tif !found {\n265|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: selection absent from source index\", ErrPlanStale)\n266|\t}\n267|\tprojection, err := (&sessstate.Projector{Repo: selected.repo, LocalHostID: reader.LocalHostID}).Project(selected.SessionID)\n268|\tif err != nil {\n269|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n270|\t}\n271|\tif projection.Winner.IsZero() {\n272|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: complete authority read proves record %s without any valid lease\", ErrBootstrapIncomplete, selected.SessionID)\n273|\t}\n274|\tlease, err := reader.winningLeaseFor(selected.SessionID)\n275|\tif err != nil {\n276|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n277|\t}\n278|\tif projection.Winner.Epoch != lease.Epoch || projection.Winner.LeaseID != lease.LeaseID {\n279|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: winning lease changed\", ErrPlanStale)\n280|\t}\n281|\tif projection.OwnerHostID != lease.HolderHostID {\n282|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: session %s carries disagreeing owner facts across lease and chain\", sessstate.ErrIntegrity, selected.SessionID)\n283|\t}\n284|\tplan := SelectionPlan{\n285|\t\tSelectorVersion:     SelectorVersion,\n286|\t\tSelector:            parsed.Raw,\n287|\t\tSessionID:           selected.SessionID,\n288|\t\tSessionRecordID:     recordID,\n289|\t\tSourceIndexDigest:   index,\n290|\t\tConfigurationDigest: configuration,\n291|\t\tLeaseRecordID:       lease.Digest,\n292|\t\tLeaseEpoch:          lease.Epoch,\n293|\t\tLeaseID:             lease.LeaseID,\n294|\t\tOwnerHostID:         lease.HolderHostID,\n295|\t\tAction:              action,\n296|\t\tDestinationHostID:   destination,\n297|\t\tExpectationDigest:   expectations,\n298|\t}\n299|\tif selected.PeerHostID == \"\" {\n300|\t\tif config.localHost == \"\" {\n301|\t\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: local host identity is required to bind a local plan source\", ErrInvalidConfig)\n302|\t\t}\n303|\t\tplan.SourceHostID = config.localHost\n304|\t} else {\n305|\t\tplan.SourceHostID = selected.PeerHostID\n306|\t\t// Null marks the local source only. An alias-less peer binds\n307|\t\t// empty: the host still distinguishes it from local.\n308|\t\talias := config.aliasFor(selected.PeerHostID)\n309|\t\taliasCopy := alias\n310|\t\tplan.SourceAlias = &aliasCopy\n311|\t}\n312|\t// The union check consults record, tombstone, and winner facts\n313|\t// only, never heads; heads are bound after the union validates.\n314|\tplan.AuthorityHeads = []string{}\n315|\tif err := reader.validateAuthorityUnion(plan, config, selected.PeerHostID); err != nil {\n316|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n317|\t}\n318|\theads, err := reader.collectAuthorityHeads(config, selected.SessionID, lease.Digest, selected.PeerHostID)\n319|\tif err != nil {\n320|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n321|\t}\n322|\tplan.AuthorityHeads = heads\n323|\tif err := checkPlanShapes(plan); err != nil {\n324|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n325|\t}\n326|\treturn plan, nil\n327|}\n328|\n329|// chainTail returns the tail event digest of a validated session chain,\n330|// or empty when the chain carries no events yet.\n331|func chainTail(repo *sessrepo.Repository, sessionID string) (string, error) {\n332|\tevents, err := repo.ListEvents(sessionID)\n333|\tif err != nil {\n334|\t\treturn \"\", err\n335|\t}\n336|\tif len(events) == 0 {\n337|\t\treturn \"\", nil\n338|\t}\n339|\treturn events[len(events)-1].EventID, nil\n340|}","final_result":true}}}
